<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    Two thirds of households have one, and for most of them the pet isn't a
    hobby — it's a dependent with a medical history, a monthly cost, a
    prescription, and no ability to tell you what hurts or when something
    changed.
  </p>
  <p>
    Which is why a pet isn't a section here. A pet is a <em>whom</em>: vet
    visits are health, food is money, the photos are already in the library,
    and teaching the dog to walk on a lead is a goal like any other.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">What each animal gets</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "A page that gathers everything") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Every appointment, receipt, note and photograph that's about Rex, in
        one place — without any of it having been filed away from where it
        also belongs.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "The care that's due") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Boosters, worming, the annual check, the medication that needs
        renewing. The same radar that watches the humans, pointed at the
        animal who can't book their own appointments.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "When the food runs out") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        From the bag size and how much they eat, the app works out roughly
        when you'll need more — and what it costs a month, which turns out
        to be a budget line most people have never actually seen.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "The vet conversation") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        The questions worth asking, the history the vet will ask you for,
        and an itemised estimate translated into what each line is actually
        for — before you agree to it in a stressful room.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">The bad days</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    A missing animal is an hour where you need a checklist rather than
    ideas: who to ring, in what order, and a poster you can print now. It's
    here because the moment you need it is the moment you can least think
    straight.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">Never a diagnosis</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    The same line the rest of Health holds. It'll talk through food,
    behaviour, routines and what's worth watching for, and it will tell you
    when something warrants a vet. It won't tell you what's wrong with your
    animal.
  </p>
</section>
